- **Real defect (high)** — `scripts/checks/lib/slice0_common.sh:27`: The new EXIT trap treats intentional timeout controls as incomplete gate results. `slice0_backends.sh:46–47` always runs the deliberately diverging `control-loop` on both backends through `observe`, which records two `incomplete` entries in the same `BOUNDED_LOG`. Even when every example and control succeeds, the trap changes exit 0 to exit 3. Thus the backend gate can never pass. Isolate the expected-timeout controls’ bounded state while still requiring their expected observations.

The other delta fixes look correct by inspection and introduce no owner-decision choice. Native Darwin/LLDB execution was not verified here.

VERDICT: ACCEPT-WITH-CHANGES
